# UI test: an inherent method declared without `public`, called from another
# file (SC0545).
#
# This is the fifth form of §4.3's rule and the only one the resolver cannot
# reach. `resolve_methods` says why in one sentence: a method "is reached
# through a receiver or through its type, never as a bare name, so it has no
# entry in any name table". `use` and a qualified path are both lookups in a
# module's table, so SC0222 can refuse them; `p.margin()` is neither, and the
# earliest phase that knows which `margin` is meant is the type checker, once
# the receiver has a type. One rule, two codes, allocated by the phase that
# detects it.
#
# What must NOT be refused is the rest of the file, and it is here for that:
# `Paper` and `Report` are public, `new` and `pages_of` carry their own
# `public`, and `report` carries none because an interface's answer is gated
# by the interface.

use shared.paper (Paper, Report)

def main():
    let p be Paper.new(3)
    print(p.pages_of())
    print(p.report())
    print(p.margin())
